DATA.points.push(...[{"id":"cd-wickware-hall","L":"gather","n":"Wickware Hall: an old country dance hall","la":45.3513,"lo":-91.7863,"y":"by 1917 (dance hall), Sunday school 1917-22","pl":"Wickware, Barron County (GNIS locality point), Maple Grove township area","co":"Barron","stt":"WI","v":"Coins 1890s-1920s, dance-hall losses: rings, earrings, pocket knives, tokens","c":"documented","s":"unknown","p":"approx","st":"History of Barron County (1922): for about five years a country church nearby had been holding interdenominational services and a Sunday school 'at the former dance hall known as Wickware Hall,' about three and a half miles northwest of the church in Maple Grove township. GNIS keeps Wickware as a locality name, and the pin is that point. The hall building is not placed.","t":"Find the hall on a 1938 air photo or an old topo near the Wickware crossroads, then work the yard, the parking ground and the paths to the road. Ask the owner first.","src":[["History of Barron County, Wisconsin (Curtiss-Wedge, 1922), church histories","https://archive.org/details/wi-barron-1922-curtiss-wedge-1"],["USGS GNIS: Wickware, Barron Co. (populated place)","https://edits.nationalmap.gov/apps/gaz-domestic/public/search/names"]],"pinconf":"C","pinev":["The 1922 history names Wickware Hall; GNIS places Wickware. The hall's lot is not fixed, so the pin can be off by a few hundred meters."]}]);

