{ const E={"cem-1833667":[{}," The Athens 1951 USGS topo: the topo draws St. Peter Church beside this cemetery (49 m), at 45.24871, -90.16751.",[["USGS Athens topographic map (1951)","https://ngmdb.usgs.gov/topoview/"]],false,""],"cem-1573616":[{}," The Granton 1954 USGS topo: the topo draws Salem Church beside this cemetery (51 m), at 44.71398, -90.37647.",[["USGS Granton topographic map (1954)","https://ngmdb.usgs.gov/topoview/"]],false,""],"pbu15-cemetery-sec-12-t38n-r15w":[{}," The Hertel 1949 USGS topo: the topo draws Evangelical Church beside this cemetery (4 m), at 45.78416, -92.155.",[["USGS Hertel topographic map (1949)","https://ngmdb.usgs.gov/topoview/"]],false,""],"cem-1568952":[{}," The River Falls 1946 USGS topo: the topo draws Mann Valley Church beside this cemetery (109 m), at 44.85939, -92.71661.",[["USGS River Falls topographic map (1946)","https://ngmdb.usgs.gov/topoview/"]],false,""],"cem-1571422":[{}," The Granton 1954 USGS topo: the topo draws Pine Circle School beside this cemetery (46 m), at 44.61264, -90.37713.",[["USGS Granton topographic map (1954)","https://ngmdb.usgs.gov/topoview/"]],false,""],"pbu15-north-dewey-school":[{}," The Hertel 1949 USGS topo: the topo draws North Dewey School 355 m from this plat spot, at 45.79845, -92.0484.",[["USGS Hertel topographic map (1949)","https://ngmdb.usgs.gov/topoview/"]],false,""],"plc06-victory-school":[{}," The La Crosse 1927 USGS topo: the topo draws Victory School 615 m from this plat spot, at 43.75477, -91.0115.",[["USGS La Crosse topographic map (1927)","https://ngmdb.usgs.gov/topoview/"]],false,""],"pli02-schoolhouse-sec-12-t31n-r5e":[{}," The Hamburg 1951 USGS topo: the topo draws Farming Dale School 736 m from this plat spot, at 45.18622, -89.81778.",[["USGS Hamburg topographic map (1951)","https://ngmdb.usgs.gov/topoview/"]],false,""],"pmo97-church-sec-26-t19n-r1w":[{}," The Wyeville 1958 USGS topo: the topo draws St. Marks Church 440 m from this plat spot, at 44.10235, -90.45469.",[["USGS Wyeville topographic map (1958)","https://ngmdb.usgs.gov/topoview/"]],false,""],"lch-1566572":[{}," Find a Grave: this was St. John's Lutheran Cemetery and \"the church is gone\"; it sits at Boss Rd and Cemetery Rd, Town of Holton (https://www.findagrave.com/cemetery/ search Christ Lutheran Cemetery, Abbotsford). A second source that a church stood here.",[["Find a Grave (read on the PC thread)","https://www.findagrave.com/"]],false,""],"lch-1569384":[{}," Find a Grave: the cemetery of the German Methodist Church in the Town of Corning, built around 1860 and disbanded before 1930 (https://www.findagrave.com/cemetery/88438/methodist-cemetery). A second source that a church stood here.",[["Find a Grave (read on the PC thread)","https://www.findagrave.com/"]],false,""],"lch-2795392":[{}," Find a Grave: German Trinity Church was founded in 1857 and merged with Saint Peter's in 1875; the Washington County Historical Society marked the old cemetery in 1989 (https://www.findagrave.com/cemetery/2449841/german-trinity-cemetery). A second source: the church site dates 1857-1875.",[["Find a Grave (read on the PC thread)","https://www.findagrave.com/"]],false,""],"pd88-m-e-church-louisville":[{}," Find a Grave (Pleasant Valley Cemetery, 300 m away): the cemetery lies on the south side of the old Louisville Methodist Church, now a private home, and the town of Louisville was given up in 1900. A second source; the building is a house now, so ask first.",[["Find a Grave (read on the PC thread)","https://www.findagrave.com/"]],false,""],"pbp77-church-sec-11-t22n-r10w":[{}," Find a Grave (Saints Peter and Paul Catholic Cemetery, 150 m away): land given by Ferdinand Theisen in 1880 for a church and graveyard; a mission of St. Boniface, Waumandee; the church was torn down in the 1950s. A second source naming the church.",[["Find a Grave (read on the PC thread)","https://www.findagrave.com/"]],false,""],"ps97-saint-bridget-church":[{}," Find a Grave (Saint Bridgets Cemetery, 140 m away): the cemetery is part of the grounds of the old Saint Bridget's Church, and the church is no longer there. A second source.",[["Find a Grave (read on the PC thread)","https://www.findagrave.com/"]],false,""],"ppo87-catholic-church-and-cemetery-milltown-se":[{}," Find a Grave (Long Lake Cemetery, first called Saint Patrick's): the church stood on one side of the cemetery and a school, now gone, on the other; the church was moved away years ago. A second source, and a lost school site beside it.",[["Find a Grave (read on the PC thread)","https://www.findagrave.com/"]],false,""],"sc-1837519":[{}," Find a Grave (Rutchow Cemetery, 240 m away, County Road U between Gilmanton and Prague): this was a growing community called Urban, with a Methodist church, a school and a cheese factory; the congregation later merged with the Montana Methodist church. A second source for the church and the hamlet.",[["Find a Grave (read on the PC thread)","https://www.findagrave.com/"]],false,""],"pp77-church-by-h-hamman-sec-18-t26n-r19w":[{}," Find a Grave (Hamman Cemetery, 44.74287, -92.71932, 560 m from this pin): \"where a German Methodist Church was once located\", burials 1868-74. A second source; the church likely stood at the cemetery, so check there before this pin's spot.",[["Find a Grave (read on the PC thread)","https://www.findagrave.com/"]],false,""]}; for(const id of []) delete LIDC[id]; addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>{ for(const p of DATA.points){ const x=E[p.id]; if(!x) continue; Object.assign(p,x[0]); if(x[3]) p.st=(p.st||"").replace(/ Air photo check \(UW[^)]*\):[^.]*\./g,"").replace(/ LiDAR cache check[^.]*\.[^.]*\./g,""); p.st=(p.st||"")+x[1]; if(x[4]) p.t=(p.t||"")+x[4]; if(x[2].length) p.src=[...(p.src||[]),...x[2]]; } }); }

